# APOLAKI — AI WORKFLOW PRD (IMPROVEMENT VERSION)

## 1. PURPOSE

Upgrade the existing assessment flow into an AI-driven decision workflow that:
- Converts user input → financial insight → action
- Adapts based on user outcomes
- Maximizes lead conversion via financing-first narrative

---

## 2. WORKFLOW MODEL

Workflow Type: Structured AI Workflow (Node-based, conditional)

FLOW:
Intent → Input → Processing → Insight → Decision → Action → Feedback → Loop

---

## 3. WORKFLOW NODES (EARS FORMAT)

---

### NODE 1 — INTENT CAPTURE

WHEN user lands on assessment page  
THE SYSTEM SHALL display financing-first hook:

- “Replace your electricity bill with a lower monthly payment”
- Example transformation (₱X → ₱Y)

AND provide CTA:
- “See My New Monthly Cost”

---

### NODE 2 — INPUT CAPTURE

WHEN user enters assessment  
THE SYSTEM SHALL collect:

- monthly_bill (required)
- location (auto-detect or dropdown)
- property_type (default residential)

AND SHALL:
- show progress indicator (Step 1–3)
- validate inputs before proceeding

---

### NODE 3 — PROCESSING (AI PERCEPTION LAYER)

WHEN input is submitted  
THE SYSTEM SHALL:

- display processing screen (2–3 seconds)
- show dynamic messages:
  - “Analyzing usage”
  - “Calculating solar potential”
  - “Optimizing monthly payment”

AND SHALL simulate intelligence perception

---

### NODE 4 — FINANCIAL MODELING

WHEN processing completes  
THE SYSTEM SHALL compute:

- system_size (kW)
- solar_payment (EMI)
- current_bill
- monthly_savings
- payback_years

CONDITION:
IF monthly_savings > 0  
→ mark as HIGH CONVERSION

ELSE  
→ mark as LOW CONVERSION

---

### NODE 5 — INSIGHT DELIVERY

WHEN results are displayed  
THE SYSTEM SHALL prioritize:

PRIMARY:
- Payment swap view:
  current_bill → solar_payment

SECONDARY:
- monthly_savings
- payback
- confidence_score

AND SHALL:
- present narrative: “You save ₱X monthly”

---

### NODE 6 — DECISION TRIGGER

WHEN user sees results  
THE SYSTEM SHALL:

IF HIGH CONVERSION  
→ show strong CTA:
   “Get My Lower Monthly Plan Installed”

IF MEDIUM  
→ show financing explanation

IF LOW  
→ show alternative messaging

---

### NODE 7 — ACTION CAPTURE (LEAD)

WHEN user clicks CTA  
THE SYSTEM SHALL collect:

- name
- phone

AND SHALL:
- assign lead_id
- store assessment linkage

---

### NODE 8 — HUMAN-IN-LOOP

WHEN lead is created  
THE SYSTEM SHALL:

- assign installer manually
- trigger contact workflow

---

### NODE 9 — FEEDBACK LOOP

WHEN lead lifecycle progresses  
THE SYSTEM SHALL capture:

- assessment_completed
- result_viewed
- cta_clicked
- lead_submitted
- conversion_status

AND SHALL:
- update model assumptions
- refine UX decisions

---

## 4. SYSTEM BEHAVIOR RULES

- Minimal input → maximal insight
- Always prioritize monthly savings over ROI
- Delay lead capture until value is shown
- Introduce perception layer (processing step)

---

## 5. SUCCESS METRICS

- Assessment completion > 70%
- CTA click > 30%
- Lead conversion > 20%

---

## 6. NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS

- Response time < 2s (excluding intentional delay)
- Mobile-first UX
- Event tracking enabled